# `@repo/brand`

Monorepo package for storefront and super-admin **logo** components (Next.js `Image` + `Link`).

## Source

- [`packages/brand/src/StorefrontLogo.tsx`](packages/brand/src/StorefrontLogo.tsx) — **`StorefrontLogo`**, image `/images/full-logo.png`.
- [`packages/brand/src/SuperAdminLogo.tsx`](packages/brand/src/SuperAdminLogo.tsx) — **`SuperAdminLogo`**, image `/Logo.png`, optional `compact` for collapsed sidebar.

Component modules use **PascalCase** filenames matching the primary export (e.g. `SuperAdminLogo.tsx`).

## App setup

1. Add `"@repo/brand": "workspace:*"` to the app `package.json`.
2. Set `transpilePackages: [..., "@repo/brand"]` in `next.config.ts`.
3. Ensure the same files exist under that app’s **`public/`** (`images/full-logo.png`, `Logo.png`) if you use the components.

## API

- Optional **`href`** (default `"/"`) on both components when the logo should navigate somewhere other than store root.

## Conventions

- Do not reintroduce duplicate logo components under `apps/frontend/src/components/Kits/`; import from `@repo/brand` instead.
- **`StorefrontLogo`** sizes the image with **intrinsic `width` / `height` and inline `style`** so it renders in apps whose Tailwind content paths do not scan `packages/brand`. Pass **`width` + `height`** (px) for fixed sizes (e.g. social header **92×58**). Next.js apps using Tailwind v4 may add `@source` to their CSS pointing at `packages/brand/src` (see `apps/social/src/app/globals.css`).
